{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cctype>\n#include <climits>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long llong;\n\nint digit_num(llong x) {\n    int cnt = 0;\n    do {\n        ++cnt;\n        x /= 10;\n    } while (x != 0);\n    return cnt;\n}\n\nllong make_rep(llong n) {\n    llong val = 0;\n    llong mult = 1;\n    llong t = n;\n    while (t) {\n        val += mult;\n        mult *= 10;\n        t /= 10;\n    }\n    if (val <= n) return val;\n    return (val - 1) / 10;\n}\n\nllong calc(llong n) {\n    if (n <= 6) return n;\n    if (n <= 11) return 13 - n;\n    \n    llong r = make_rep(n);\n    llong next_r = r * 10 + 1;\n    \n    if (n % r == 0) {\n        llong k = n / r;\n        if (n <= next_r / 2 + r) {\n            return digit_num(r) * k;\n        } else {\n            return digit_num(next_r) + calc(next_r - n);\n        }\n    } else {\n        llong lo = (n / r) * r;\n        llong hi = lo + r;\n        llong ans = calc(lo) + calc(n - lo);\n        if (n > next_r / 2) {\n            llong alt = digit_num(hi) + calc(hi - n);\n            ans = (alt < ans) ? alt : ans;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    llong n;\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << calc(n) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef digit_num(x):\n    cnt = 0\n    if x == 0:\n        return 1\n    while x != 0:\n        cnt += 1\n        x //= 10\n    return cnt\n\ndef make_rep(n):\n    val = 0\n    mult = 1\n    t = n\n    while t:\n        val += mult\n        mult *= 10\n        t //= 10\n    if val <= n:\n        return val\n    return (val - 1) // 10\n\ndef calc(n):\n    if n <= 6:\n        return n\n    if n <= 11:\n        return 13 - n\n    \n    r = make_rep(n)\n    next_r = r * 10 + 1\n    \n    if n % r == 0:\n        k = n // r\n        if n <= next_r // 2 + r:\n            return digit_num(r) * k\n        else:\n            return digit_num(next_r) + calc(next_r - n)\n    else:\n        lo = (n // r) * r\n        hi = lo + r\n        ans = calc(lo) + calc(n - lo)\n        if n > next_r // 2:\n            alt = digit_num(hi) + calc(hi - n)\n            ans = alt if alt < ans else ans\n        return ans\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    n = int(input())\n    print(calc(n))\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.42901024245657e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006923967972397804, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -6.615896563744172e-05, -0.000301673193462193, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.000609927112236619, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5769888162612915, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00012385078298393637, 0.0, -5.149708886165172e-05, -1.9550132492440753e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.013220862485468388, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.02642119862139225, 0.0, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.384